Hooray! After more than 2 years of playing nethack I finally ascended a
character. Funny, my first acsension should be a tourist, as I don't
play the class very often.

Wonderin, the neutral Tourist started his Quest for the Amulet with a
protection run. He found a magic whistle early. He made it to minetown
at XL1, and got lucky, naked AC of 1. Minetown had 3 magic lamps and
was coaligned too. So Wonderin rubbed his lamps, and got Speed Boots,
GDSM and a tame djinn ("Sorry, I'm all out of whishes!"). He also wrote
a + of Identify early on, which worked surprisingly well. The first sac
gave Magicbane, and the Silver Saber he used as a main Weapon before
turned out to be enchanted to +2. #twoweaponing these fine blades he
then proceeded trough Soko, which gave him a much needed BoH and
cleared out the bottom of the mines. A Bones gave him serious trouble
on his way to mines end, the Body of a player seems to have risen from
the dead as a humn mummy. These hit harder than ghosts!

One problem was the complete absence of means of levitation and
reflection, so he swam to Medusas, and just whacked her with a Towel
around his head. The Perseus statue then finally gave levitation boots.
The Castle was a breeze with conflict, and gave the Wand of Wishing.
So, wished for "oReflection, Magic Marker, Helm of Brilliance and the
Eye of the Aethiopica.

On to the quest. Tourist quest is fun and all went smooth with = of
stealth and / of death. Got the Bell and the blessed Platinum Yendorian
Express Card. Now, with nothing left to do in the dungeon of doom,
wonderin was reluctant to enter Gehennom at first. So he tried Pudding
farming. Uh, oh. Farming is too much work for a Tourist! This he
realized quickly, and stopped. It gave him Mjollnir and werebane
though, which he both stashed away and never used.

He then started polypiling, which gave him 6(!) "oLS. Unfortunately,
while trying to get some better gloves than leather, he polyed his
levitation boots. And still no = of levitation or other means to move
in the air. But when his last / of Polymorph exploded, he decided to
visit Vlad, and get on with the Quest for the Amulet. Vlad really is a
wimp. With 2 out of 3 invocation items, Wonderin went back to his stash
and got ready for rodney. Enchanting SDSM for reflection (MR from
Magicbane, PYEC) turned the scales to dust, so +2 SDSM was the last
wish from the Castle wand, which then exploded.

Now he went to Rodney's, killed him, took the Book of the Dead and
c?ofTele levelported to the Bottom of Hell, where he had marked the
vibrating square before. Killed the Priest and ran. Myterious force
kicked in 3 or 4 times, Wonderin just kept on being really lucky in
this game. So he ran upwards, back to his stash on level 2 to grab all
the things needed for the planes. Still no means of levitation, but
mrivan from #nethack pointed him to the possibility of polying into a
Vampire Lord for the planes of Air and Water. Got into toubles on air.
Two Jabberwocks and other Monsters brought him back to 3 hp and human
form, leaving him unable to move. 3rd prayer in the entire game sorted
him out, and he charmed the monsters. Then he relaxed in a steam
vortex, until he could Poly into a V again. Proceeded to astral, whith
slight difficulties of finding the magic portal on the water plane.

On Astral he relied on =of Conflict and / of Teleport to clear his
path. He had to deal with famine, which he had to zap with a / of death
two times and death, who just died somehow. Went to the altar in the
middle first, which was chaotic. Then turned to the left. Conflict
killed Death for me, I only saw his purple corpse. Went into the
temple, beamed away the Archon there (/oTele rules!) and offered the
Amulet. YES!

Wonderin, neutral male human Tourist



